@rekram1-node, since you are assigned to this issue, I would appreciate your thoughts on whether this capability should be limited to tool.execute.before or exposed as a reusable plugin-level requester.

I think this is somewhat important since opencode lacks os-level enforcement of permission settings. Exposing this capability would leave room for sandbox and policy plugins to provide that enforcement cleanly in the future.

I may not have time (also experience) to participate deeply in the API design in the near term, but I wanted to document the runtime-sandbox requirement before the V2 plugin boundary becomes fixed. I would be happy to provide additional details about the Landstrip use case later if useful.

@sdivens it's not the same and I believe does not cover the requirement. I may want to extend only one paste. A prompt may consist of multiple big pastes.

